    "created_at": "2025-06-27T01:17:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-27T01:18:09Z",
    "body": "This is similar to https://github.com/whatwg/infra/issues/518.\n\nI have always considered it equivalent to throwing. It seemed pretty obvious to me that, while some algorithms straddle both worlds, the translation between them is pretty clear. ECMAspeak returns throw completions / normal completions, web standards throw exceptions / return values, and there's no relationship that makes sense here other than 1:1.\n\nIn particular, it feels unnecessary to me to have explicit conversion steps at the boundaries which do things like:\n\n- Catch webby-algorithm exceptions / return values and convert them into returning completions in the host hooks, or\n- Inspect a value returned from an ECMAScript AO and convert it from a normal completion to a value, or from a throw completion into a step which rethrows the exception.\n\nHowever, it seems like we've confused at least two people with this, so maybe it's not as obvious as I thought, and we'd benefit from conversion steps like this.",
