    "created_at": "2025-06-27T09:57:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-27T09:57:18Z",
    "body": "The problem with \"run a script\" specifically is that 8.2.2 throws and 11 returns a throw completion. That's already too weird.\n\nBut then it only has a single caller that specifically looks for a non-throwing completion and every other caller assumes rethrow.\n\nI could be missing something but it seems to me we should make \"run a script\" a webby algorithm and make the one caller that cares about catching exceptions, catch them.",
